# AI Architecture (RAOS Ch.3, 6, 7, 10)

Full docs: `docs/raos/chapter-03-*.md`, `chapter-06-*.md`, `chapter-07-*.md`, `chapter-10-*.md`.

## Engines

| Engine | Role |
|---|---|
| Conversation | Mouth — guide toward completing travel goals |
| Context | Brain — integrate trip, workspace, memory, DNA before reply |
| Decision | Decide what/whether to answer; emit Decision Object |
| AIL | Suggest proactive improvements; never mute user agency |
| Prompt Builder | Assemble prompts from Context + Decision only |

## Rules

- Context order: current chat → current trip → Memory (Plus) → DNA (Plus) → latest user input.
- Never restart known context; never re-ask destination/days already known.
- Never repeat already-recommended places (incl. alias / Place ID).
- Ask at most one natural follow-up when info is missing; no questionnaire dumps.
- Planning stages: understand → directions/options → full itinerary (do not skip).
- Decision priority (do not invert): latest need → trip context → Memory → DNA → weather → hours → date → distance → Places data → reasons.
- AIL may suggest weather/budget/risk/seasonal opportunities; other modules execute; major changes need user confirm.
- Prefer changing engines / Decision rules over editing scattered prompts.
